cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Lunar Lander RL: a reproducible benchmark of Q-learning, DQN and REINFORCE"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible reinforcement-learning experiments on Gymnasium's LunarLander-v3. Tabular-style
  Q-learning with tile coding, DQN and REINFORCE, implemented from scratch, are compared with
  Stable-Baselines3 DQN and PPO at an equal budget of one million environment steps, with ten
  seeds per method, held-out test episodes and bootstrap confidence intervals. The repository
  includes a replication study of an earlier version, ablations and a wind-robustness study,
  and regenerates every reported number, table and figure from logged runs.
authors:
  - family-names: Kowal
    given-names: Bart
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bartkw12/lunar-lander-rl"
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - lunar lander
  - DQN
  - Q-learning
  - REINFORCE
  - PPO
  - reproducibility
  - gymnasium
